    id: "iit-madras-school-connect-2026-guide",
    slug: "iit-madras-school-connect-2026-guide",
    title: "IIT Madras School Connect 2026: A useful opportunity for Classes 9–12",
    excerpt: "Students in Classes 9 to 12 can now apply for the October 2026 cohort of IIT Madras School Connect. Explore future-focused subjects and earn an e-certificate from IIT Madras CODE.",
    category: "Education News",
    readTime: "4 min read",
    date: "Sep 14, 2026",
    author: "Growtopper Team",
    authorAvatar: "https://api.dicebear.com/9.x/notionists/svg?lips=&seed=IIT&backgroundColor=e8d5f5",
    image: "/images/og-iit-madras.png",
    content: `<p>Students in Classes 9 to 12 can now apply for the <strong>October 2026 cohort of IIT Madras School Connect</strong>. The eight-week online programme introduces school students to future-focused subjects and helps them make more informed decisions about higher education and careers. Applications are open until <strong>30 September 2026</strong>, and courses are scheduled to begin on <strong>5 October 2026</strong>.</p><h2>What is IIT Madras School Connect?</h2><p>School Connect is an online outreach programme conducted by the <strong>IIT Madras Centre for Outreach and Digital Education (CODE)</strong>.</p><p>The programme allows school students to explore academic fields that may not be taught in depth at school. It is especially useful for students who are unsure about which stream, degree or career path to choose after Class 10 or Class 12.</p><p>IIT Madras has also opened the programme to Class 9 students, giving them more time to explore different subjects before making important academic decisions.</p><h2>Who can apply?</h2><p>The programme is open to students studying in:</p><ul><li>Class 9.</li><li>Class 10.</li><li>Class 11.</li><li>Class 12.</li></ul><p>Students can apply through the official IIT Madras CODE website at <a href="https://code.iitm.ac.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">code.iitm.ac.in</a>.</p><h2>Important dates</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg"><thead class="bg-gray-50"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold text-brand-dark uppercase tracking-wider">Event</th><th scope="col" class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold text-brand-dark uppercase tracking-wider">Date</th></tr></thead><tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200"><tr><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Application deadline</td><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500">30 September 2026</td></tr><tr><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Course commencement</td><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500">5 October 2026</td></tr><tr><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Course duration</td><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500">Eight weeks</td></tr><tr><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Mode</td><td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500">Online</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Students should complete registration before the deadline because late applications may not be accepted.</p><h2>Subjects and disciplines offered</h2><p>The programme offers courses across <strong>17 academic disciplines</strong>, including:</p><ul><li>Data Science and Artificial Intelligence.</li><li>Aerospace.</li><li>Cybersecurity.</li><li>Electronic Systems.</li><li>Chemical Engineering.</li><li>Molecular Engineering.</li><li>Architecture and Design.</li><li>Product Design.</li><li>Law.</li><li>Economics and Finance.</li><li>Humanities.</li><li>Ecology.</li><li>Digital Humanities.</li><li>Game Technology.</li><li>Mathematics and Computing.</li><li>Engineering Biological Systems.</li></ul><p>This broad selection allows students from different interests and academic backgrounds to explore fields beyond the usual Science, Commerce and Humanities choices.</p><h2>How are the courses conducted?</h2><p>The eight-week programme includes:</p><ul><li>Pre-recorded lectures.</li><li>Live sessions.</li><li>Assignments.</li><li>Computer-based assessments.</li></ul><p>Courses are available in <strong>English and Hindi</strong>, which may make the programme accessible to students from a wider range of backgrounds.</p><h2>Certificate from IIT Madras CODE</h2><p>Students who complete the required course activities will receive an official <strong>e-certificate from the IIT Madras Centre for Outreach and Digital Education</strong>.</p><p>Students should carefully follow the attendance, assignment and assessment requirements because certificate eligibility may depend on completing the prescribed activities.</p><h2>Why should students consider joining?</h2><h3>Helpful for stream selection</h3><p>Students in Classes 9 and 10 can explore different subjects before deciding whether to choose Science, Commerce, Humanities or a vocational pathway.</p><h3>Useful for career planning</h3><p>Students in Classes 11 and 12 can gain an early understanding of possible degree programmes and careers.</p><h3>Exposure to emerging fields</h3><p>The programme includes areas such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, aerospace, game technology and digital humanities, which students may not otherwise study at school.</p><h3>Learning from an IIT ecosystem</h3><p>The programme gives students academic exposure connected with IIT Madras and helps them understand how university-level learning differs from school-level education.</p><h2>Special recognition opportunity</h2><p>Students and teachers from top-performing schools may be invited to the IIT Madras campus for a felicitation ceremony. They may also receive an opportunity to interact with IIT Madras faculty and other members of the institute.</p><p>This recognition is subject to the programme’s performance criteria and official selection rules.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Students should follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Visit <a href="https://code.iitm.ac.in/schoolconnect/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">code.iitm.ac.in/schoolconnect/</a></li><li>Find the October 2026 School Connect cohort.</li><li>Check the eligibility and course details.</li><li>Select a preferred discipline.</li><li>Complete the registration form.</li><li>Upload or enter the required information.</li><li>Submit the application before 30 September 2026.</li><li>Save the confirmation and course-access details.</li></ol><p>Students should use only the official IIT Madras CODE website and avoid relying on unverified registration links.</p><h2>What students should check before applying</h2><p>Before submitting the application, students should confirm:</p><ul><li>Whether the course is suitable for their class.</li><li>Course language.</li><li>Schedule of live sessions.</li><li>Assignment and assessment requirements.</li><li>Any applicable fee.</li><li>Certificate eligibility conditions.</li><li>Device and internet requirements.</li><li>Whether the programme will fit alongside school studies.</li></ul><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>IIT Madras School Connect 2026 is an important opportunity for K–12 students who want to explore subjects and careers before making major academic decisions. With 17 disciplines, bilingual courses, online learning and an IIT Madras e-certificate, the programme can be particularly valuable for students in Classes 9–12.</p><p>Applications close on <strong>30 September 2026</strong>, and the courses begin on <strong>5 October 2026</strong>. Students should verify all current details and register through the official IIT Madras CODE website.</p>`
